<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction govt bonds of HUF16bln on Dec 5.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction govt bonds of HUF16bln on Dec 5.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction two-year government bonds, 1998/K series, worth 16 billion forints nominally on December 5, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday in a statement.</p>
<p>    Date of issue		 3 October, 1996</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	    3 October, 1998</p>
<p>    Bills on offer		16,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	   100.09 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum yield		 22.49 pct</p>
<p>Average yield</p>
<p>     at previous auction	21.99 pct (Nov 7)</p>
<p>NOTE - The 1998/K bond bears a fixed interest of annual 21.5 percent, to be paid twice a year (Apr 3 and Oct 3).</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
